     ccrruunncchhiiddee — hides symbol names from ld, for crunching programs together

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ccrruunncchhiiddee [--ff _k_e_e_p_-_l_i_s_t_-_f_i_l_e] [--kk _k_e_e_p_-_s_y_m_b_o_l] [_o_b_j_e_c_t_-_f_i_l_e _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccrruunncchhiiddee utility hides the global symbols of _o_b_j_e_c_t_-_f_i_l_e such that
     they are ignored by subsequent runs of the linker, ld(1).  Some symbols
     may be left visible via the --kk _k_e_e_p_-_s_y_m_b_o_l and --ff _k_e_e_p_-_l_i_s_t_-_f_i_l_e options.
     The _k_e_e_p_-_l_i_s_t_-_f_i_l_e must contain a list of symbols to keep visible, one
     symbol per line.  The names given by _k_e_e_p_-_s_y_m_b_o_l or in _k_e_e_p_-_l_i_s_t_-_f_i_l_e
     should be C names.  For example, to keep the C function “foo” visible,
     the option “-k foo” should be used.

     The ccrruunncchhiiddee utility is designed as a companion program for
     crunchgen(1), which automates the process of creating crunched binaries
     from multiple component programs.

